  "keyTakeaways": [
    "U.S. plastics exports were $77.66B in 2025 (−3.0%); polyethylene resin (3901, $16.51B) and finished articles (3926, $9.30B) lead.",
    "Mexico and Canada took 46% of exports and charge nothing on qualifying goods, but Canada has surtaxed six consumer-plastic items at 50% since September 8, 2026.",
    "The EU's tariff on U.S. plastics fell from 6.5% to zero on July 1, 2026 under Regulation (EU) 2026/1455.",
    "China is the one big buyer that raised tariffs — a 10% extra duty on all U.S. goods and a 74.9% anti-dumping duty on U.S. POM copolymer — and U.S. exports there fell 19.7% to $5.98B."
  ],
